      "versionNonce": 91296026,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793981796269,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> In a microservice architecture we can have different services like NodeJS, Redis and Postgres \nrunning on different containers but within a Network.\n-> We will expose only the NodeJS Public IP to the world nodejs will talk to redis and postgres via private IP.",
      "rawText": "-> In a microservice architecture we can have different services like NodeJS, Redis and Postgres \nrunning on different containers but within a Network.\n-> We will expose only the NodeJS Public IP to the world nodejs will talk to redis and postgres via private IP.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> In a microservice architecture we can have different services like NodeJS, Redis and Postgres \nrunning on different containers but within a Network.\n-> We will expose only the NodeJS Public IP to the world nodejs will talk to redis and postgres via private IP.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false
    },
