    {
      "id": "G4V2r4Sg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 155.93996178188195,
      "y": 1143.7683594769856,
      "width": 534.01663175717,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 374949382,
      "version": 109,
      "versionNonce": 1939335962,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793983051342,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> User-defined bridges provide automatic DNS\nresolution between containers.\n-> User-defined bridges provide better isolation.\n-> Containers can be attached and detached from\nuser-defined networks on the fly.\n-> Each user-defined network creates a configurable\nbridge.\n-> Containers can communicate with each other using\ncontainer names.",
      "rawText": "-> User-defined bridges provide automatic DNS resolution between containers.\n-> User-defined bridges provide better isolation.\n-> Containers can be attached and detached from user-defined networks on the fly.\n-> Each user-defined network creates a configurable bridge.\n-> Containers can communicate with each other using container names.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> User-defined bridges provide automatic DNS resolution between containers.\n-> User-defined bridges provide better isolation.\n-> Containers can be attached and detached from user-defined networks on the fly.\n-> Each user-defined network creates a configurable bridge.\n-> Containers can communicate with each other using container names.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false
    },
    {
      "id": "I6N3A08V",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -561.3550226126266,
      "y": 1136.9875101862976,
      "width": 660.4502549482371,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0c",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1880204186,
      "version": 290,
      "versionNonce": 41781766,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793983009145,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> Linked containers on the default bridge network share\nenvironment variables.\n-> Containers on the default bridge network can communicate using\nIP addresses.\n-> Containers cannot resolve each other by container names\nautomatically.\n-> Containers must be connected to the same bridge network to\ncommunicate directly.\n-> Port mapping (-p) is required to access container services from\nthe host machine.\n-> Provides less isolation and flexibility compared to user-defined\nbridge networks.",
      "rawText": "-> Linked containers on the default bridge network share environment variables.\n-> Containers on the default bridge network can communicate using IP addresses.\n-> Containers cannot resolve each other by container names automatically.\n-> Containers must be connected to the same bridge network to communicate directly.\n-> Port mapping (-p) is required to access container services from the host machine.\n-> Provides less isolation and flexibility compared to user-defined bridge networks.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> Linked containers on the default bridge network share environment variables.\n-> Containers on the default bridge network can communicate using IP addresses.\n-> Containers cannot resolve each other by container names automatically.\n-> Containers must be connected to the same bridge network to communicate directly.\n-> Port mapping (-p) is required to access container services from the host machine.\n-> Provides less isolation and flexibility compared to user-defined bridge networks.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CDGNGN0f",
