    {
      "id": "kdwTe7DI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -417.1588217159226,
      "y": 3349.6844215414853,
      "width": 1262.5406286036764,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 201138374,
      "version": 513,
      "versionNonce": 571888838,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793991687535,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-> ipvlan: IPvlan networks give users total control over both IPv4 and IPv6 addressing.\nThe VLAN driver builds on top of that in giving operators complete control of layer 2 VLAN\ntagging and even IPvlan L3 routing for users interested in underlay network integration. \n\n-> macvlan: Macvlan networks allow you to assign a MAC address to a container, making it\nappear as a physical device on your network. The Docker daemon routes traffic to\ncontainers by their MAC addresses.\n\n-> none: Completely isolate a container from the host and other containers. none is not\navailable for Swarm services.",
      "rawText": "-> ipvlan: IPvlan networks give users total control over both IPv4 and IPv6 addressing. The VLAN driver builds on top of that in giving operators complete control of layer 2 VLAN tagging and even IPvlan L3 routing for users interested in underlay network integration. \n\n-> macvlan: Macvlan networks allow you to assign a MAC address to a container, making it appear as a physical device on your network. The Docker daemon routes traffic to containers by their MAC addresses.\n\n-> none: Completely isolate a container from the host and other containers. none is not available for Swarm services.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-> ipvlan: IPvlan networks give users total control over both IPv4 and IPv6 addressing. The VLAN driver builds on top of that in giving operators complete control of layer 2 VLAN tagging and even IPvlan L3 routing for users interested in underlay network integration. \n\n-> macvlan: Macvlan networks allow you to assign a MAC address to a container, making it appear as a physical device on your network. The Docker daemon routes traffic to containers by their MAC addresses.\n\n-> none: Completely isolate a container from the host and other containers. none is not available for Swarm services.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false
    }
  ],
